  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building up civil society for constructive engagement in national development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD, in conjunction with other international donors and the government of Timor Leste, provides regular funding support to FONGTIL, the national NGO Forum.   Specific requirements towards which FONGTIL is working are: a clear law on non-profit organisations which includes NGOs, a clear definition of the role of NGOs, and clear local agreements about NGO participation.  FONTIL also seeks to help its members improve their skills in monitoring and evaluation, and plays a co-ordinating role to facilitate their collaborative engagement at both local and national levels.  Under the current strategic plan, CAFOD support is directed particularly towards efforts to strengthen relationships between the member NGOs, and between the NGOs and the national government, so as to encourage and facilitate NGO participation with development plans at national and local levels.</narrative>
  </description>
